  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "In two different experiments, an object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> moving with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> hits two different walls and comes to rest within<br />(i) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math> second, (ii) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> seconds, respectively.<br />Choose the correct option out of the following :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "INjvY",
      "text": "Impulse and average force acting on the object will be same for both the cases.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "emoCb",
      "text": "Impulse will be same for both the cases but the average force will be different.",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "GGarc",
      "text": "Average force will be same for both the cases but the impulse will be different.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cWuJB",
      "text": "Average force and impulse will be different for both the cases.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Impulse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Change in momentum</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, in both the cases the impulse is same.</p><p>Average force is defined as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>avg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Since the time in the two cases is different, the average force will be different.</p></blockquote>",
